      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/claude-charming-lamport-a61w1n/cat-harness/process/Process_DocsSite",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns/Process",
      "name": "Publishing the docs site, and keeping the previews alive",
      "summary": "Builds the docs site from this checkout's sources and publishes it to `gh-pages` (`.github/workflows/docs-site.yml`).",
      "description": "Builds the docs site from this checkout's sources and publishes it to `gh-pages` (`.github/workflows/docs-site.yml`). Publishing replaces `gh-pages` wholesale: anything on the branch that this build did not produce is gone unless restored, so the open pull requests' staging previews are copied in before the replace and checked on the deployed branch after it. The site is published whatever the built-site checks find: they run before the push and are judged after it, so a finding turns the run red with the site already live. A refused security gate or a failed deploy stops the run, and a check that could not tell counts as a failure (`ci-health`). Every failure, from a refused security gate to a lost preview or a failed check, goes through one alert to the publication manager, and the next clean publish closes it. Mechanical throughout; there is no human lane.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn",
      "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness/blob/main/sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn",
